"text": " Most goalkeepers stop the ball with their hands. This one used his heels. Upside down. September 6, 1995. Wembley, England against Colombia. Just a friendly. What could possibly go wrong? In goal for Colombia, Rene Higuita. His nickname? El Loco. The madman. Jamie Redknapp tries a lob from 30 yards. A soft, easy ball. Any keeper would just catch it. Not Higuita. He dives forward, flips his legs over his head and kicks it away with his heels. 20,000 people at Wembley had never seen anything like it. And the funniest part? The flag was already up for offside. He didn't even need to save it. It wasn't luck either. He later said he'd practiced it all through the warm-up. The match ended nil-nil. Nobody remembers the score. Would you try this in goal? Tell me in the comments.",
